🚀 Week 3 – Day 4 OOP Concepts & Class/Object Creation in Java ☕

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Java is an **Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)** language.

OOP helps in:

✔ Organizing code into reusable components
✔ Improving maintainability
✔ Modeling real-world entities

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 1. What is OOP?

Object-Oriented Programming is a programming approach based on:

* Classes
* Objects
* Encapsulation
* Inheritance
* Polymorphism
* Abstraction

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🏗️ 2. What is a Class?

A class is a **blueprint** for creating objects.

It defines:

* Data (fields/variables)
* Behavior (methods)

---

📌 Example Class

```java id="c1"
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " " + age);
    }
}
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 3. What is an Object?

An object is a **real instance of a class**.

Each object has:

* State (data)
* Behavior (methods)

---

📌 Creating Objects

```java id="c2"
Student s1 = new Student();
Student s2 = new Student();
```

---

📝 Assigning Values

```java id="c3"
s1.name = "Saakshi";
s1.age = 21;
```

---

▶️ Calling Methods

```java id="c4"
s1.display();
```

---

💻 Complete Example

```java id="c5"
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " - " + age);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student();
        s1.name = "Saakshi";
        s1.age = 21;

        Student s2 = new Student();
        s2.name = "Rahul";
        s2.age = 22;

        s1.display();
        s2.display();
    }
}
```

